## Session 48 summary

**Build `8B767DA4`** carries all of this session's fixes (write-side proven correct; read-side partial).

### Write-side durable lost-update — FIXED & PROVEN
The 2/tcp `cache_coherency`/uv failure was a durable write-side lost-update: a node's committed dir deletes never reached the LUN, so the peer cold-read the stale disk. Proven via raw O_DIRECT dir-block parse + a new cross-node `P-WRACT` active-count+realns write trace. Two gaps, both fixed:
1. **Block-format deletes** — restored contention-gated publish-before-notify in `mxfs_dlm_dir_durable_signal` (v0.5.1 had gutted it to publish-only). Gated on `i_dlm_dir_gen>0`. Hit a 150s self-deadlock first (caller holds dp i_lock WRITE → `down_read_trylock` spins) → fixed by calling the flush directly (ILOCK_EXCL already guarantees fork stability).
2. **Shortform deletes** — the dir converts block→shortform as it shrinks; `mxfs_dlm_dir_inode_durable` was gated `!self_created`, skipping the `mkdir -p`'d (self-created) uv dir. Changed to `!self_created || gen>0`.

**Proof it's fixed:** raw inode read = `di_format=01` (shortform, 0 files), byte-identical on both initiators; `drop_caches` on the outlier → it sees 0.

### Read-side residual — isolated to the storage layer
After the write-side fix the outlier still serves stale (~2/3 prod). Added reload-on-`gen>loaded` to lookup+readdir (0/3→1/3). Remaining root, refined via `P133-DINO-READSTALE` firing **0×** + dd-fresh-only-seconds-later: **a stale SCST per-initiator READ cache** serves the outlier the old inode cluster during the test window; even "coherent" plain-bdev reads see it; `fua_disable=0` doesn't pierce it. `dirwr=1` passing is a timing artifact — must validate in production.

